  "description": "The SAML\u202fIdP profile named **ExampleSPProfile** is configured for the service provider at **https://sp.example.com/** (service provider ID\u202fhttps://sp.example.com/ and audience\u202fhttps://sp.example.com/). Assertions are posted to the consumer service endpoint **https://sp.example.com/SAML2/SSO/POST**, while the single\u2011sign\u2011out URL is **https://sp.example.com/logout**. The issuer is identified as **https://sp.example.com/issuer**, and the name\u2011ID is derived from the user\u2019s email (expression\u202fuser.email) using the\u202femailAddress format. All unsigned requests are rejected (rejectunsignedrequests\u202fON), and passwords are never sent (sendpassword\u202fOFF). Metadata is retrieved from **https://idp.example.com/metadata**, imported successfully (metadataimportstatus\u202fSUCCESS), and refreshed every\u202f1440\u202fminutes. The default authentication group for this profile is **SAMLUsers**.\n\nAttribute release is defined for sixteen attributes, each using the Basic format: the user\u2019s **email** (Email Address) is taken from\u202fuser.email, **givenName** (First Name) from\u202fuser.firstName, **sn** (Last Name) from\u202fuser.lastName, **displayName** (Full Name) from\u202fconcat(user.firstName, ' ', user.lastName), **uid** (User ID) from\u202fuser.username, **memberOf** (Group Membership) from\u202fuser.groups, **department** (Department) from\u202fuser.department, **title** (Job Title) from\u202fuser.title, **telephoneNumber** (Phone Number) from\u202fuser.phone, **mobile** (Mobile Phone) from\u202fuser.mobilePhone, **postalAddress** (Address) from\u202fuser.address, **employeeNumber** (Employee Number) from\u202fuser.employeeId, **organizationName** (Company) from\u202fuser.company, **birthDate** (Date of Birth) from\u202fuser.dateOfBirth, **gender** (Gender) from\u202fuser.gender, and **locale** (Locale) from\u202fuser.locale. Security settings specify a SHA256 digest method, assertion encryption **ON** with AES256 and RSA\u2011OAEP for key transport, and signing of both the assertion and response (**BOTH**) using RSA\u2011SHA256 through the signature service **SignatureService1**. The SAML binding for authentication requests is POST, the logout binding is also POST, and the signing certificate versions are v1 for the IdP (IdPCert) and v2 for the SP (SPCert). The allowed clock skew is 300\u202fseconds.",
  "reference_json": {
